# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts and the Dockerfile must keep LF whatever the checkout platform
# does: a `.sh` file with CRLF endings fails on macOS and Linux with a confusing
# "bad interpreter" error, because the carriage return becomes part of the
# shebang path. PowerShell is the mirror image and prefers CRLF.

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
